**Handoff:**

No backend changes are required for Taiga #13. The spec/design's core design decision is to implement the undo window entirely in `App.jsx` by deferring the `DELETE` API call for 5 seconds rather than firing it immediately — since the task is only hidden from view (not mutated or removed from state) during that window, undo is a pure frontend state operation. `backend/app/main.py`, `backend/app/store.py`, and `frontend/src/api.js` are all reused unmodified.

I ran no commands and made no edits, since there is nothing in this scope to implement. The frontend-scope developer instance (working on `App.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, new `UndoToast.jsx`, `App.css`) owns the entire feature. No backend tests need updating either, since the existing `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}` route's behavior (including its 404-on-missing semantics, which AC6 relies on) is unchanged.